00:26:14.800 --> 00:26:15.660
And you're bullish.

00:26:16.460 --> 00:26:17.560
You're better off waiting.

00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:20.240
You need that to stabilize.

00:26:20.560 --> 00:26:21.500
Before you actually commit.

00:26:23.340 --> 00:26:24.740
So instead of buying it here.

00:26:25.660 --> 00:26:26.700
On huge volume.

00:26:27.020 --> 00:26:27.920
And being stopped out.

00:26:28.240 --> 00:26:28.460
Here.

00:26:29.260 --> 00:26:30.860
You buy it for the same price here.

00:26:31.280 --> 00:26:32.880
When you've got the momentum to the
upside.

00:26:38.100 --> 00:26:39.220
When there's low volume.

00:26:40.500 --> 00:26:41.480
What if you're bearish?

00:26:44.380 --> 00:26:45.880
It's a great signal if you're bearish.

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:47.580
Get short.

00:26:51.260 --> 00:26:52.420
Relative strength index.

00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:53.620
Who knows about this?

00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:02.060
So the average of the previous.

00:27:02.800 --> 00:27:04.500
Market convention is 14 days.

00:27:06.360 --> 00:27:08.840
The average of the up closing prices.

00:27:10.040 --> 00:27:12.840
And the average of 14 days down closing
prices.

00:27:13.260 --> 00:27:13.780
Indexed.

00:27:21.160 --> 00:27:23.580
So standard RSI measures will tell you
that.

00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:25.480
If it goes over an index level of 70.

00:27:26.300 --> 00:27:27.300
It's overbought.

00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:32.120
If it goes under an index level of 30.

00:27:33.400 --> 00:27:34.360
It's oversold.

00:27:37.900 --> 00:27:38.640
But that's.

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:40.380
Completely the wrong way to look at it.

00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:44.240
Because the stock.

00:27:44.500 --> 00:27:45.680
Can be above 70.

00:27:45.820 --> 00:27:46.500
Or even 80.

00:27:46.620 --> 00:27:47.240
Or even 90.

00:27:47.380 --> 00:27:47.880
On the index.

00:27:48.560 --> 00:27:49.780
And just go sideways.

00:27:50.520 --> 00:27:51.100
In price.

00:27:51.920 --> 00:27:53.380
And then the index can go down to 50.

00:27:54.120 --> 00:27:55.680
So the price might never come down.

00:27:56.760 --> 00:27:57.900
So it's not overbought.

00:27:59.340 --> 00:28:00.240
And inversely.

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:01.080
It's not oversold.

00:28:01.280 --> 00:28:02.560
That's the wrong way of defining.

00:28:03.060 --> 00:28:04.540
In terms of what's happening.

00:28:05.120 --> 00:28:06.000
In words.

00:28:07.140 --> 00:28:08.540
It's the wrong way of looking at it.

00:28:11.320 --> 00:28:16.700
What's happened when the index level of an
RSI goes above 70, 80, 90 and is really
strong.

00:28:17.200 --> 00:28:19.080
It's just confirming your bullish view.

00:28:21.480 --> 00:28:23.200
And you could actually miss the trade.

00:28:23.200 --> 00:28:29.620
So you have to combine it with other
technicals.

00:28:29.860 --> 00:28:30.960
It's a momentum indicator.

00:28:31.520 --> 00:28:35.680
Combine it with the technicals of trend
that we've just looked at.

00:28:36.140 --> 00:28:36.240
Yeah.

00:28:37.100 --> 00:28:40.200
And make up your mind whether it's a good
