00:28:42.540 --> 00:28:44.840
Because short-term momentum just confirms
your view.

00:28:49.040 --> 00:28:52.780
And the asset might never ever come down
in price.

00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:54.640
But the RSI can.

00:28:55.700 --> 00:28:57.380
Just the momentum becomes slower.

00:28:57.540 --> 00:28:58.340
But it keeps going up.

00:29:00.600 --> 00:29:01.240
Make sense?

00:29:06.360 --> 00:29:08.700
What about moving averages?

00:29:10.780 --> 00:29:13.040
So we can use exponential moving averages.

