Would have actually cut the 10-day moving
average.

00:30:20.500 --> 00:30:20.920
From below.

00:30:22.200 --> 00:30:24.760
So when you get those crosses in the
moving averages.

00:30:25.120 --> 00:30:26.060
It confirms.

00:30:27.180 --> 00:30:27.900
Your view.

00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:29.640
If your view is that it's going that way.

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:31.600
But it denies your view.

00:30:31.900 --> 00:30:32.600
If you think.

00:30:32.980 --> 00:30:35.020
If you think it's going the other way.

00:30:37.580 --> 00:30:39.140
Again you're going to have your
fundamental.

00:30:40.400 --> 00:30:40.920
Predisposition.

00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:43.360
So you can either hang back.

00:30:43.600 --> 00:30:44.340
Or participate.

00:30:45.720 --> 00:30:46.820
You are the gatekeeper.

00:30:47.100 --> 00:30:47.660
Nobody else.

00:30:53.020 --> 00:30:56.400
What are the moving averages that we use
in the stock market?

00:30:56.400 --> 00:30:56.440
What are the moving averages that we use
in the stock market?

00:31:05.320 --> 00:31:07.920
Has anybody ever heard of a golden cross?

00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:12.400
Anybody ever heard of that?

