00:37:56.220 --> 00:37:58.080
So be the gatekeeper to your own capital.

00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:02.420
That's the first screening test.

00:38:02.920 --> 00:38:03.140
TA.

00:38:05.580 --> 00:38:06.760
Okay, welcome back.

00:38:07.120 --> 00:38:15.720
So, we just went through, at the
presentation, technical analysis as part
of the gatekeeping process.

00:38:17.100 --> 00:38:30.000
Now, when we go through TA, we obviously
are looking at it as one of the most
important timing indicators to good ideas
and also stopping us from putting on bad
ideas.

00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:48.380
So, the whole point of this really is to
use TA as a tool to add value to our idea,
as in to turn an idea into a good trade,
because a good idea might not necessarily
be a good trade.

00:38:49.380 --> 00:38:56.380
You can end up being stopped out on a good
idea, because you've mistimed it, and then
you'll prove to be right.

00:38:56.660 --> 00:38:58.220
We've been through this a few times now.

00:38:59.400 --> 00:39:05.020
Probably the most important thing here is
your fundamental predisposition.

00:39:06.080 --> 00:39:19.180
So, when you go through the world view,
the industry view, the stock view, and you
arrive at the gatekeeping process, and
your idea is ready to be turned into a
trade, potentially,

00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:28.640
you're going to have a fundamental
predisposition, and probably the worst
mistake you can ever make is to then pull
up the chart and then change your mind.

00:39:29.420 --> 00:39:30.420
Just forget about it.

00:39:31.140 --> 00:39:43.560
You're going to have lots of ideas coming
